<title>SINGAPORE: India's Hindustan assessing damage on Kandla jetty.</title>
<headline>India's Hindustan assessing damage on Kandla jetty.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The extent of damage suffered by Hindustan Petroleum Corp Ltd's floating jetty at the Indian west-coast port of Kandla should be known in about one week's time, a company official said.</p>
<p>&quot;We have divers going down now. It will take another three to four days before we know how much time it would take (to repair the jetty),&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Hindustan owns one of two floating jetties closed earlier this week after a collision involving two tankers.  </p>
<p>The official said he understood the other jetty, owned by Indian Oil Corp (IOC), suffered less damage and could be operational in one to two weeks.</p>
<p>A spokesman for IOC said he could not comment.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
